WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.980
<b><i>We look the same, but men call us monsters. 

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.130
We still don't know who's behind it.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.020
What is that thing, anyway?

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.980
<b><i>Utsutsu Dreams of Hell</i></b>

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:13.330
I still can't believe that a castle 
appeared out of nowhere!

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.780
This isn't just Kishuu's problem anymore!

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.590
They say that the former followers

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.280
of the Toyotomis, to the west, 
may rise up, as well...

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.660
How terrifying. They truly say that?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.540
Impossible...

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:36.050
I am currently seeking to learn 
if it truly is "impossible."

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.560
Raise your head.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:47.780
The lord has been feeling ill, of late.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.320
Today, for once, he has felt better.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.190
So know that you are lucky to see him at all.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.440
Yes, sir! I am honored!

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.240
Wait, Hachirou...

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.610
Where are you going?

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.830
I told you not to be concerned for me.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.380
But then, what just happened...

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.710
You cared about what happened to us.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.150
True.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:25.350
You could say that only a coward sees 
what is right and fails to do it.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.600
The samurai love to say that, right?

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.230
Let's let Hachirou do as he pleases.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.200
We still have a job to do.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.400
Stay safe.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:54.120
I slowed you down again, huh?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.800
If you were slowing me down, 
I wouldn't take you.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.040
I'm taking you because I 
want you to be useful.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.280
True... I'll take you up on that.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.420
They're here.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.650
So it seems.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:21.400
I guess drawing all the Rain 
away was impossible, huh?

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.010
Too many to explain it that way.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.490
There was another unit.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.540
Did Shichigen check before 
he gave the signal?

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.540
You're a man. Stop whining.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.790
Take care of this.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.520
It's more valuable than your life.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.800
That's a crappy way for a 
woman to cheer a man up.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.670
I'm not trying to cheer you up.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.560
I was telling the truth.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:19.820
Oh, no!

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:31.870
Saizou!

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.270
The stuff you were carrying?!

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.390
Whatever it was, it's not more 
important than your life.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.190
Utsutsu,

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.790
show me one of your illusions.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:47.630
I can reflect the illusions my 
eyes see into other eyes.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:54.570
Even in this smoke, I can spread 
your illusions everywhere.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:06:00.170
If you see one of my illusions, 
you'll be drawn inside it, too!

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.310
I'm not going to see it.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.160
My eyes will.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.420
How is that different?!

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:08.390
My eyes are just a passage.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.360
There's no other way.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.690
I'll do it.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.450
Even if I start burning, don't stop.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.200
I won't!

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.690
It worked!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:03.480
Saizou?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.730
Saizou!

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.100
How much time has passed?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.770
Just a little.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.810
There's still plenty of time.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:43.510
I see...

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:54.260
I already see too much.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:57.160
So as a rule, I don't look at 
things I don't need to see.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.550
I don't even dream.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:02.670
The opposite of me.

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:06.250
I can't see what I want to see.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.630
So my dreams have only been terrible.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.680
I'll get the cannon.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.470
You stay here.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:24.100
That illusion of yours was 
a nasty thing, though.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:30.330
I can't imagine what had to happen for 
you to want to show someone that.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:45.840
Father!

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.210
Father!

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:52.590
Father...

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:12.020
All the jet-black night, 
he comes to me in dreams...

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:16.740
All the jet-black night, 
he comes to me in dreams...

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.220
Ever since I was very little,

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:22.490
I spent half the month in 
that dark storehouse,

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:28.000
with the mandala, unsure whether 
it was training or punishment.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.290
What's wrong?

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:01.630
I want to see something prettier, 
even if just in my dreams.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.040
You dream?

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:07.690
Yes, I do!

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:11.490
But they're scary dreams.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:13.670
I'm sure that's...

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:18.680
Hell.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.140
That isn't the poem's beginning.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:26.220
"It seems my heart wants 
me to die of this longing.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.660
All the jet-black night...

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.910
He comes to me in dreams, to keep 
my hopeless passion burning."

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.370
That's hard to understand.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.070
Um...

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:40.320
The speaker falls in love with 
someone in dreams, and dies.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.540
It may only be a love poem,

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:46.060
but there's an aspect of truth to it.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.940
Dreams can kill.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.430
Emotions can kill.

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.960
At their extreme, they become 
a ninja technique.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:01.000
A technique that can only 
be learned in youth.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.060
The time is coming.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:15.480
Master it by the next 
cherry-blossom blooming.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.490
What happens then?

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.780
The hour of destiny.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:25.370
The time when you will no longer be young.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:29.540
If you fail to master the technique,

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.970
all of this will have been for naught.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.290
You will have to die.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:44.010
That is the way of Dreaming Reality, Utsutsu.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.610
I don't care! I'm not scared!

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.210
I see. You aren't frightened?

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.900
Think I'm trying to scare you?

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:02.910
Poor girl...

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.560
This is your Dreaming Reality?

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:35.850
Yes.

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:40.940
You would call that worthless 
technique Dreaming Reality?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.980
This is the end.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.470
<i>I'm going to be killed...</i>

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.100
Father!

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:17.090
My kimono has been soaked in oil.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.860
These flames won't disappear 
until it burns to ash.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.360
Father!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.180
I cannot kill my daughter.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:29.440
But do not mistake this for pity.

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:35.850
You must live with the fact that you killed 
your father, rather than yourself!

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.980
This hell will remain forever in your head!

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:46.160
Make that emotion into your technique.

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.840
Ninja Technique: Dreaming Reality.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.310
Hey, let's go.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:52.070
It's hard to believe this thing 
runs off whale whiskers.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:59.710
That Hadaebou guy...

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.600
How much can we trust him?

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:04.960
A skilled shinobi in Tenkai's service.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.440
What is there to trust?

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:10.770
Indeed...

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:11.470
What?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:15.860
No, I was just thinking that we're similar.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:17.360
Yeah.

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:22.980
We're both trying to see how much we can 
use the other for our own advantage.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:26.730
Well, we'll be the ones to ultimately win.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.850
I certainly hope so.

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:32.240
Either way, never lower 
your guard around him.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:05.930
So the plan was to get yourself inside 
by taking advantage of this chaos?

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:14.910
Is that why you had all of them help?

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:34.900
Let's go.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:45.590
Tch.

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:46.650
You suck.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.940
You really thought we'd 
hit it the first time?

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.440
We have three bombs.

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:55.310
But this also told the enemy our location.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:59.110
As we speak, the Rain will be heading for us.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.330
Take care of them, when they do.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.710
What are you doing?

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:08.960
I can't bear to watch.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.100
Hibiki?

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:13.210
You, too?

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:17.090
We can't win without her power now.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.720
So, an all-out fight, huh?

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:22.220
We'll keep watch around you.

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:29.980
What's that?

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:33.490
I fire it into that hole.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:37.650
And your bomb will follow it.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:39.740
Is that possible?

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.860
If you're good enough.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:16.840
Run!

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:41.220
I thought the Rain would suffice 
to handle the likes of you.

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:47.820
l give you compliments for making 
me work, if nothing else...

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.380
What happened?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.480
This is what that damned 
priest was talking about.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.030
The technique to reverse time's flow.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.530
<b>The Inverted Halberd of Time</b>

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.530
The Inverted Halberd of Time.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:03.530
Is that really possible?

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:08.470
I'm starting to doubt what my 
own eyes just showed me.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.040
I can't believe it.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:15.090
But time really moved backward!

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:17.550
Then, that's...

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:21.010
Kujaku Tsuibamu?

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.260
Is this the one we're fighting?

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:31.560
The Five Treasures and Five Flowers 
were defeated by these people.

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:37.190
Hachisu, where's the cannon?

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:38.850
Right here.

00:19:38.850 --> 00:19:41.800
Your Gorouza can still be used, right?

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:46.080
Of course. But how?

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.160
I don't know.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:51.330
But it's all we've got.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.390
We have to do something with it!

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:57.960
Hadaebou.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:02.040
It's almost amazing how you 
never cease to be sneaky.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.840
A compliment. Thank you.

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:08.040
And? What will you do when 
you're in the Murakumo alone?

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:10.230
Kill Joujin?

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:16.270
There are very few excuses that will 
allow me to pass, aren't there?

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:18.730
Let's hear it.

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:23.240
If it's entertaining enough, 
I will let you pass.

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:30.010
Tadanaga-sama was kidnapped 
by Joujin, perhaps.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:32.600
Tadanaga was taken by Joujin?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.750
Why?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.380
That's what I'm going to find out.

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:40.380
But what power does Tadanaga have now?

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:43.880
He has no position, and no 
followers who admire him.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.490
No soldiers, either.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:49.780
What is it that Tenkai fears?

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:55.490
Why would Tenkai care if Joujin had him?

00:20:56.220 --> 00:20:58.650
A horrible thing to say of such a man, but...

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:04.040
Suruga-sama is still Suruga-sama.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.280
That will never change, no matter what.

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:08.860
I see.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:13.160
Tadanaga is the grandson of the 
deceased Shogun Ieyasu.

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:16.770
The perfect puppet.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:25.120
And your job is to save him before 
that happens, Hadaebou.

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:30.430
If you don't hurry, people will 
begin to make a fuss.

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:31.810
Yes.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.560
We can't use a double forever.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:39.940
If he cannot be saved, 
his life is to be taken.

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:45.950
That is what Tenkai told you to do, yes?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.010
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:30.010
He looked and saw a sword.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:32.620
Above it, he saw swirling clouds.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.010
Thus, he named this sword Ama no Murakumo.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:38.020
<b><i>Murakumo Must Be Destroyed</i></b>

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:39.280
Murakumo, meaning a "gathering of clouds."
